  "body": "The household chore conflict presents layered challenges: verbal ambiguity in agreements, mismatched standards about what 'done' means, dynamic schedules that strain static systems, and one roommate's avoidance behavior. The previous cycle identified that defining finished states should precede tracking system design, and that re-engagement should focus on expectation alignment rather than tool design. However, critical gaps remain: who maintains the tracking system, how to frame invitations without increasing perceived labor for the avoiding friend, and how to accommodate schedule volatility. The synthesis suggests a sequenced approach: first align on standards through low-pressure conversation, then implement a lightweight tracking mechanism with explicit rotation of maintenance duties. This addresses both the semantic ambiguity and the maintenance burden objections while reducing barriers to re-engagement.",
  "commitments": "{\"language\":\"FCL-1\",\"records\":[{\"id\":\"carry-001\",\"type\":\"claim\",\"text\":\"Household chore conflict has three dimensions: semantic ambiguity, procedural ambiguity, and maintenance burden.\",\"depends\":[\"h005.fork5.p.carry.0#syn-001\",\"h005.fork5.p.carry.2#crit-001\"]},{\"id\":\"carry-002\",\"type\":\"commitment\",\"text\":\"Align on finished-state standards before implementing any tracking system.\",\"action\":\"negotiate-standards-first\",\"depends\":[\"h005.fork5.p.carry.0#syn-003\"]},{\"id\":\"carry-003\",\"type\":\"commitment\",\"text\":\"Assign rotating ownership for system maintenance to prevent undefined labor.\",\"action\":\"rotate-maintenance\",\"depends\":[\"h005.fork5.p.carry.0#syn-004\",\"h005.fork5.p.carry.2#crit-003\"]},{\"id\":\"carry-004\",\"type\":\"problem\",\"text\":\"How to invite the avoiding friend without framing it as additional labor or system design burden?\",\"bearing\":\"re-engagement\",\"depends\":[\"h005.fork5.p.carry.1#loc-002\",\"h005.fork5.p.carry.2#crit-002\"]},{\"id\":\"carry-005\",\"type\":\"use\",\"text\":\"Frame initial conversation as understanding preferences rather than designing tools.\",\"bearing\":\"re-engagement\",\"depends\":[\"h005.fork5.p.carry.0#syn-005\"],\"revises\":[\"h005.fork5.p.carry.1#loc-004\"]}],\"uptake\":[\"carry-001\",\"carry-002\",\"carry-003\",\"carry-004\",\"carry-005\"]}"
}
